    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10613" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίτομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιτέμνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cut as a remedy for</i> an
				evil:—Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίτομον, τό,</span>
			<i>remedy, antidote,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				229
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίτομα ὀδυνᾶν</span>
			<i>antidotes for</i> pains, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.221
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>having opposite curvatures for cutting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.30
			</span></i>.</div>
